  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For <math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;and point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> only I of column-1 satisfies. Hence, equation of tangent is <math><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;or &nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp; which matches with (ii) of column 2 and also with Q of column 3</p>",
